{% extends '../layouts/default.twig' %}

{% set head_title = 'Overview' %}

{% block page %}
    <nav class="main-navigation">
        <a href="#what">what</a>
        <a href="#how">how</a>
        <a href="#code">code</a>
    </nav>
    <header>
        <div id="header-content" class="header-content">
            <div class="logo-container">
                {% include "../components/logo.twig" %}
            </div>
            <div class="title-container">
                <h1 class="title">
                    <span class="text-red">A</span>rbitrary
                    <span class="text-red">R</span>emote
                    <span class="text-red">C</span>ontrol
                    <span class="text-blue">S</span>ystem
                </h1>
                <h2 class="subtitle">
                    Multi-Device Interactive Web Based VR
                </h2>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>
    <section class="row">
        <div
          class="column"
          id="what"
        >
            <img
              class="section-artwork"
              src="../../assets/images/generative_lines_1.png"
              alt="abstract line artwork"
            >
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="title-container">
                <h3 class="title text-red">Connect Multiple Devices</h3>
                <h4 class="subtitle">Smartphones, Tablets, Laptops, Desktop PCs, Fridges</h4>
            </div>
            <p>
                If it has an internet connection, it can be used to control your virtual experience.
            </p>
            <p>
                Make use of an abstract API to connect any device. Your users can use one smartphone as a headset
                and a second one as a controller, or combine their desktop or laptop PCs to use keyboard
                and mouse inputs.
            </p>
            <p>
                The controlling application does not have to be browser-based. All it needs is a connection to the
                internet.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
        <div
          class="column"
          id="how"
        >
            <img
              class="section-artwork"
              src="../../assets/images/generative_lines_2.png"
              alt="abstract line artwork"
            >
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="title-container">
                <h3 class="title text-red">Peer-To-Peer Connectivity</h3>
                <h4 class="subtitle">The most direct way for cross-devices communication.</h4>
            </div>
            <p>Once a broker server has established a connection between your devices, they will communicate directly
                with each other. This reduces your need for remote servers to a bare minimum.</p>
            <p>
                Using an MQTT broker
                server, your application can gracefully fall back to using the minimalistic and fast MQTT protocol, if
                Peer-To-Peer WebRTC is not possible or available.</p>
            <p>
                Create your <span class="text-red">ARC</span><span class="text-blue">S</span>
                MQTT cloud server right now, starting
                at 3,50€ / Month. You can also self-host and manage it using following one of the MQTT installation
                guides.
            </p>
            <a class="link" href="#">
                <img class="chevron" src="../../assets/images/chevron.png">
                <span>See cloud hosting options</span>
            </a>
            <div>
                <a class="link" href="#">
                    <img class="chevron" src="../../assets/images/chevron.png">
                    <span>See self hosting instructions</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
        <div
          class="column"
          id="code"
        >
            <img
              class="section-artwork"
              src="../../assets/images/generative_lines_3.png"
              alt="abstract line artwork"
            >
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="title-container">
                <h3 class="title text-red">Tested & Extensible UX/UI</h3>
                <h4 class="subtitle">Well-Engineered Flows for Connection and Onboarding</h4>
            </div>
            <p>Use, reuse and adapt any combination of our existing UX flows and UI components.</p>
            <p>We provide code examples, documentation for remote control UIs, Quality of Life features, onboarding
                flows and error handling.</p>
            <p>Jump right into one of the Vue.js A-Frame and Three.js templates, or pick
                single components from the modular Repository architecture.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="imprint">
        Barthélémy Bonhomme <span class="text-blue">//</span> Hans-Böckler-Straße 28
        <span class="text-red">//</span> 53225 Bonn — This page saves no data, no cookies, and doesn't track you.
    </footer>
{% endblock %}
